A TABLE ROW STANDS OR FALLS WHOLE. The host reads a row only where a line opens on a pipe at its
first column and ends on a pipe carrying at most one of `f`, `h`, `c` or `k`. A line failing that
builds no row, and it ends the table above it. Nothing here opens a region, so nothing here can
colour what follows it.

|a row that never closes

|a |row missing its last pipe

|a |row |carrying an unknown marker |b

|a |row |carrying a capital marker |H

  |a row opened after two spaces |

  |a class row opened after two spaces |k

|

A prose line, and a row-shaped line directly under it that the paragraph keeps.
|a |b |

|a |b |
A prose line directly under a table row, which the table does not keep.

A RAGGED TABLE STILL BUILDS. The host pads nothing and refuses nothing, so each row carries the cells
it writes.

|one |two |three |
|one |
|one |two |three |four |

AN EMPTY ROW STILL BUILDS. Two pipes make a row holding one empty cell.

||
||||

A MARK WITH NOTHING TO JOIN. A `<` opening a row finds no cell before it and reads as text.

|<|a colspan-left mark with no cell before it |

A `>` closing a row finds no cell after it, and the host hands the cell before it a span of one.

|a |>|

A `~` in the first row finds no row above it, and the host drops the cell.

|~|a rowspan mark with no row above it |

THE HOST SKIPS SPACES BEFORE A HEADING MARK AND NOTHING ELSE, so a tab leaves the `!` as text. THE
TWO REGEX ENGINES ALSO PART WAYS HERE — this line's own tab reads differently under the WASM
Oniguruma build and its JavaScript translation, the one control character in this corpus where
they disagree, so it carries its own `BEHAVIOUR` ruling in `corpus/engine-ledger.txt` rather than
crossing to the second engine unremarked like everything else here.

|	!a tab before the heading mark |x |

THREE MARKS WHERE TWO WERE MEANT. `^^` opens superscript, and a third `^` hands the first one back to
vertical alignment. The same holds for `,`.

|^^^three carets^^ |,,,three commas,, |
